/Title (3.2 Cross-Site Scripting \(XSS\) Attack  AstoredXSSattackwastested by adding a note containing a script payload such as <script>alert\('XSS'\)</script>. The goal of this attack was to make the browser execute JavaScript when the note is displayed.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 248 0 R
/Next 267 0 R
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Title (5. Mitigation Techniques  Thefollowing mitigation techniques were used to prevent or reduce the tested vulnerabilities:)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 268 0 R
/Next 249 0 R
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Title (Expected result: The attack should fail because the template engine escapes user input. The script should appear as plain text and should not run in the browser.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 265 0 R
/Next 269 0 R
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
