269 0 obj
<<
/Title (3.3 Brute Force Attack  A brute-force attack was tested by repeatedly trying different incorrect passwords for the same account. The purpose of this attack was to see whether unlimited login attempts could eventually allow an attacker  to guess the password.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 267 0 R
/Next 272 0 R
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Title (Expected result: The attack should fail because the registered password follows a stronger password  policy and because repeated failed attempts can trigger account lockout.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 273 0 R
/Next 268 0 R
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Title (XSS)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 268 0 R
>>
endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Title (Expected result: The attack should fail or be slowed down because the system tracks failed login attempts and temporarily locks the account after repeated failures.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 269 0 R
/Next 273 0 R
>>
endobj
273 0 obj
<<
/Title (3.4 Dictionary Attack  Adictionary attackwastested by trying common password guesses such as password, 12345678, qwerty, admin123, and other weak passwords. This attack checks whether weak or predictable passwords can be guessed easily.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 272 0 R
/Next 270 0 R
>>
endobj
